                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets just fix the input if we can to make it only have printable characters?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Unless I am missing something obvious, I am not picking up what you mean by \"input\"... Do you mean fixing those blobs under `examples/` (and/or the generator)? Something along the lines of\n\n```diff\n \t//Ensure the FRU text is not null terminated early.\n \tfor (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n \t\t// FRU string can only be ASCII\n-\t\tdescriptor->FruString[i] = rand() % 127 + 1;\n+\t\tdescriptor->FruString[i] = rand() % (0x80 - 0x20) + 0x20;\n```\n\n(and everywhere ASCII is mentioned) and rerun the tests with `GEN_EXAMPLES = 1`? Or do you mean, replacing all the non-printable characters in the output json with another replacement characters?\n\nEither way, I tried stuff but roundtrip tests don't seem to be happy with what I am trying to do. It's late here so I will try again some time later."
                },
